# OpenShift 4.22 — Production Operator Reference
## Purpose, Installation and Base Configuration for Each Operator

Companion to *OCP BareMetal Disconnected Install Guide*. All operators are installed through OLM from the mirrored catalog `cs-redhat-operator-index-v4-22` (namespace `openshift-marketplace`). Replace with `redhat-operators` on a connected cluster.

---

## 0. Common installation pattern

Every operator below is installed with the same three objects. Only the values in the per-operator table change.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: <NAMESPACE>
  labels:
    openshift.io/cluster-monitoring: "true"     # lets platform Prometheus scrape it
---
apiVersion: operators.coreos.com/v1
kind: OperatorGroup
metadata:
  name: <NAME>
  namespace: <NAMESPACE>
spec:
  targetNamespaces:                              # OMIT this block for "AllNamespaces" scope
    - <NAMESPACE>
---
apiVersion: operators.coreos.com/v1alpha1
kind: Subscription
metadata:
  name: <PACKAGE>
  namespace: <NAMESPACE>
spec:
  name: <PACKAGE>
  channel: <CHANNEL>
  source: cs-redhat-operator-index-v4-22
  sourceNamespace: openshift-marketplace
  installPlanApproval: Manual                     # production default
```

Workflow:
```bash
oc apply -f <operator>.yaml
oc get installplan -n <NAMESPACE>                                   # Manual approval
oc patch installplan <ip-name> -n <NAMESPACE> --type merge -p '{"spec":{"approved":true}}'
oc get csv -n <NAMESPACE> -w                                        # wait for Succeeded
# discover channel:
oc get packagemanifest <PACKAGE> -n openshift-marketplace -o jsonpath='{.status.defaultChannel}'
```

Scope rule: **Single namespace** operators (OperatorGroup with `targetNamespaces`) manage CRs only in their own namespace. **All namespaces** operators (no `targetNamespaces`) watch the whole cluster. Use the scope listed for each operator — using the wrong one causes `OperatorGroup`/`InstallMode` errors.

Infra placement: operators that run heavy workloads (ODF, Loki, Prometheus, Tempo) take `nodeSelector`/`tolerations` in their primary CR so they land on infra nodes:
```yaml
nodeSelector:
  node-role.kubernetes.io/infra: ""
tolerations:
  - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoSchedule}
  - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoExecute}
```

