## 1. Storage

### 1.1 Local Storage Operator (LSO)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Discovers local disks on nodes and exposes them as PersistentVolumes (block or filesystem). On bare metal it is the layer ODF consumes for its OSDs. Also useful for databases that need local NVMe. |
| **Package** | `local-storage-operator` |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-local-storage` / single namespace |
| **Channel** | `stable` |
| **Primary CRs** | `LocalVolumeDiscovery`, `LocalVolumeSet`, `LocalVolume` |

Configuration:
```yaml
# Discover disks on storage nodes (optional but useful)
apiVersion: local.storage.openshift.io/v1alpha1
kind: LocalVolumeDiscovery
metadata: {name: auto-discover-devices, namespace: openshift-local-storage}
spec:
  nodeSelector:
    nodeSelectorTerms:
      - matchExpressions:
          - {key: cluster.ocs.openshift.io/openshift-storage, operator: In, values: [""]}
---
# Auto-claim matching disks as block PVs
apiVersion: local.storage.openshift.io/v1alpha1
kind: LocalVolumeSet
metadata: {name: odf-disks, namespace: openshift-local-storage}
spec:
  nodeSelector:
    nodeSelectorTerms:
      - matchExpressions:
          - {key: cluster.ocs.openshift.io/openshift-storage, operator: In, values: [""]}
  storageClassName: localblock
  volumeMode: Block
  fstype: ""
  maxDeviceCount: 4
  deviceInclusionSpec:
    deviceTypes: [disk]
    deviceMechanicalProperties: [NonRotational]
    minSize: 500Gi
  tolerations:
    - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoSchedule}
    - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoExecute}
```
Verify: `oc get localvolumediscoveryresults -n openshift-local-storage -o yaml`, `oc get pv | grep localblock`.
Production notes: use `deviceInclusionSpec` filters so OS disks are never claimed; label storage nodes before applying; disks must be raw (no partitions/filesystems).

### 1.2 OpenShift Data Foundation (ODF)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Software-defined storage (Ceph + NooBaa) delivering RBD block (RWO), CephFS (RWX) and S3 object storage inside the cluster. Required by the internal registry, Loki, OADP, Quay, etc. in disconnected environments with no external storage array. |
| **Packages** | `odf-operator` (pulls `ocs-operator`, `mcg-operator`, `odf-csi-addons-operator`, `rook-ceph-operator`, `cephcsi-operator`, `odf-prometheus-operator`, `recipe`, `ocs-client-operator`) |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-storage` / single namespace (namespace label `openshift.io/cluster-monitoring: "true"` required) |
| **Channel** | `stable-4.22` |
| **Primary CRs** | `StorageSystem`, `StorageCluster`, `ObjectBucketClaim` |
| **Alternative** | Vendor CSI (NetApp Trident, Portworx, Dell PowerFlex/PowerStore) when an external array exists — install from the certified catalog and skip LSO/ODF. |

Configuration (after LSO PVs exist on ≥3 nodes):
```yaml
apiVersion: ocs.openshift.io/v1
kind: StorageCluster
metadata: {name: ocs-storagecluster, namespace: openshift-storage}
spec:
  manageNodes: false
  monDataDirHostPath: /var/lib/rook
  flexibleScaling: true                 # allow uneven disk counts per node
  resources: {}                         # or set mds/mon/osd requests for predictable sizing
  encryption:
    clusterWide: true                   # at-rest OSD encryption (recommended)
  placement:
    all:
      tolerations:
        - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoSchedule}
        - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoExecute}
  storageDeviceSets:
    - name: ocs-deviceset
      count: 2                          # disks per node
      replica: 3
      portable: false
      dataPVCTemplate:
        spec:
          storageClassName: localblock
          accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]
          volumeMode: Block
          resources: {requests: {storage: "1"}}
```
Post-config:
```bash
oc get storagecluster -n openshift-storage        # Phase: Ready
oc get cephcluster -n openshift-storage           # HEALTH_OK
oc get sc                                          # ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd / -cephfs / openshift-storage.noobaa.io
oc patch sc ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd -p '{"metadata":{"annotations":{"storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class":"true"}}}'
oc patch sc ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd -p '{"allowVolumeExpansion":true}'
```
Production notes: minimum 3 storage nodes × 16 vCPU / 64 GB for the ODF pods alone; dedicate SSD/NVMe; monitor `CephClusterWarningState` alert; enable `clusterWide` encryption before data is written (cannot be enabled later).

