## 2. Logging & Observability

### 2.1 Red Hat OpenShift Logging + Loki Operator

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Logging operator deploys the **Vector** collector (DaemonSet) and manages log forwarding. Loki Operator deploys **LokiStack**, the horizontally-scalable log store backed by S3. Together they replace the deprecated EFK (Elasticsearch/Fluentd/Kibana). Logs are viewed in the console via the Cluster Observability Operator UI plugin. |
| **Packages** | `cluster-logging` (ns `openshift-logging`, single namespace) and `loki-operator` (ns `openshift-operators-redhat`, **all namespaces**) |
| **Channels** | `stable-6.4` (Logging 6.x — check `defaultChannel`) |
| **Primary CRs** | `LokiStack`, `ClusterLogForwarder` (`observability.openshift.io/v1`), `UIPlugin` (via COO) |

Configuration:
```yaml
# 1. S3 bucket from NooBaa
apiVersion: objectbucket.io/v1alpha1
kind: ObjectBucketClaim
metadata: {name: loki-bucket, namespace: openshift-logging}
spec: {generateBucketName: loki, storageClassName: openshift-storage.noobaa.io}
```
```bash
# 2. Secret for Loki from the OBC
BUCKET=$(oc get obc loki-bucket -n openshift-logging -o jsonpath='{.spec.bucketName}')
KEY=$(oc get secret loki-bucket -n openshift-logging -o jsonpath='{.data.AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID}' | base64 -d)
SECRET=$(oc get secret loki-bucket -n openshift-logging -o jsonpath='{.data.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY}' | base64 -d)
oc create secret generic logging-loki-s3 -n openshift-logging \
  --from-literal=bucketnames=$BUCKET --from-literal=endpoint=https://s3.openshift-storage.svc:443 \
  --from-literal=access_key_id=$KEY --from-literal=access_key_secret=$SECRET --from-literal=region=noobaa
oc get cm openshift-service-ca.crt -n openshift-logging || \
  oc create cm openshift-service-ca.crt -n openshift-logging --from-literal=service-ca.crt="$(oc get cm openshift-service-ca.crt -n openshift-config -o jsonpath='{.data.service-ca\.crt}')"
```
```yaml
# 3. LokiStack
apiVersion: loki.grafana.com/v1
kind: LokiStack
metadata: {name: logging-loki, namespace: openshift-logging}
spec:
  size: 1x.small                          # 1x.medium for >100 nodes
  storage:
    schemas: [{version: v13, effectiveDate: "2024-10-01"}]
    secret: {name: logging-loki-s3, type: s3}
    tls: {caName: openshift-service-ca.crt}
  storageClassName: ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd
  tenants: {mode: openshift-logging}
  limits:
    global:
      retention: {days: 30}
      ingestion: {ingestionRate: 10, ingestionBurstSize: 20}
  template:
    compactor:    &p {nodeSelector: {node-role.kubernetes.io/infra: ""}, tolerations: [{key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoSchedule},{key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoExecute}]}
    distributor:  *p
    gateway:      *p
    indexGateway: *p
    ingester:     *p
    querier:      *p
    queryFrontend: *p
    ruler:        *p
---
# 4. Collector service account and RBAC
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata: {name: collector, namespace: openshift-logging}
```
```bash
for r in collect-application-logs collect-infrastructure-logs collect-audit-logs logging-collector-logs-writer; do
  oc adm policy add-cluster-role-to-user $r -z collector -n openshift-logging; done
```
```yaml
# 5. Forwarder
apiVersion: observability.openshift.io/v1
kind: ClusterLogForwarder
metadata: {name: collector, namespace: openshift-logging}
spec:
  serviceAccount: {name: collector}
  managementState: Managed
  collector:
    resources: {limits: {memory: 2Gi}, requests: {cpu: 200m, memory: 512Mi}}
  outputs:
    - name: default-lokistack
      type: lokiStack
      lokiStack:
        target: {name: logging-loki, namespace: openshift-logging}
        authentication: {token: {from: serviceAccount}}
      tls: {ca: {key: service-ca.crt, configMapName: openshift-service-ca.crt}}
    - name: corp-siem                     # optional external SIEM
      type: syslog
      syslog: {url: "tls://siem.example.com:6514", rfc: RFC5424, facility: local0, severity: informational}
  pipelines:
    - name: to-loki
      inputRefs: [application, infrastructure, audit]
      outputRefs: [default-lokistack]
    - name: audit-to-siem
      inputRefs: [audit]
      outputRefs: [corp-siem]
```
Verify: `oc get lokistack -n openshift-logging`, `oc get ds collector -n openshift-logging`, console → Observe → Logs.
Production notes: audit logs are **not** collected by default — the pipeline above adds them; size the S3 bucket for `retention × daily volume × 1.3`; set `ingestionRate` to avoid dropping logs.

### 2.2 Cluster Observability Operator (COO), Tempo, OpenTelemetry

| Operator | Package / ns / scope | Channel | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Cluster Observability Operator** | `cluster-observability-operator` / `openshift-cluster-observability-operator` / all ns | `stable` | Deploys console **UIPlugins** (logging, troubleshooting panel, distributed tracing, monitoring), standalone `MonitoringStack` Prometheus instances for teams, and Perses dashboards. Required to view Loki logs and Tempo traces in the console. |
| **Red Hat build of OpenTelemetry** | `opentelemetry-product` / `openshift-opentelemetry-operator` / all ns | `stable` | Manages `OpenTelemetryCollector` instances to receive, process, and export traces/metrics/logs from apps (OTLP). Acts as the ingestion gateway for Tempo. |
| **Tempo Operator (Distributed Tracing)** | `tempo-product` / `openshift-tempo-operator` / all ns | `stable` | Deploys `TempoStack`/`TempoMonolithic` — S3-backed distributed trace store replacing Jaeger. |

Configuration:
```yaml
# COO UI plugins
apiVersion: observability.openshift.io/v1alpha1
kind: UIPlugin
metadata: {name: logging}
spec:
  type: Logging
  logging: {lokiStack: {name: logging-loki}, logsLimit: 50, timeout: 30s}
---
apiVersion: observability.openshift.io/v1alpha1
kind: UIPlugin
metadata: {name: troubleshooting-panel}
spec: {type: TroubleshootingPanel}
---
apiVersion: observability.openshift.io/v1alpha1
kind: UIPlugin
metadata: {name: distributed-tracing}
spec: {type: DistributedTracing}
---
# Tempo (needs an OBC + secret like Loki, in ns openshift-tracing)
apiVersion: tempo.grafana.com/v1alpha1
kind: TempoStack
metadata: {name: tracing, namespace: openshift-tracing}
spec:
  storageSize: 20Gi
  storage: {secret: {name: tempo-s3, type: s3}, tls: {enabled: true, caName: openshift-service-ca.crt}}
  storageClassName: ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd
  retention: {global: {traces: 168h}}
  tenants:
    mode: openshift
    authentication: [{tenantName: prod, tenantId: 1610b0c3-c509-4592-a256-a1871353dbfa}]
  template:
    gateway: {enabled: true}
    queryFrontend: {jaegerQuery: {enabled: true}}
---
# OpenTelemetry collector gateway
apiVersion: opentelemetry.io/v1beta1
kind: OpenTelemetryCollector
metadata: {name: otel, namespace: openshift-tracing}
spec:
  mode: deployment
  replicas: 2
  serviceAccount: otel-collector
  config:
    receivers:
      otlp: {protocols: {grpc: {endpoint: 0.0.0.0:4317}, http: {endpoint: 0.0.0.0:4318}}}
    processors:
      batch: {}
      memory_limiter: {check_interval: 1s, limit_percentage: 75}
    exporters:
      otlp:
        endpoint: tempo-tracing-gateway.openshift-tracing.svc:8090
        tls: {insecure: false, ca_file: /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/service-ca.crt}
        auth: {authenticator: bearertokenauth}
        headers: {X-Scope-OrgID: prod}
    extensions:
      bearertokenauth: {filename: /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token}
    service:
      extensions: [bearertokenauth]
      pipelines:
        traces: {receivers: [otlp], processors: [memory_limiter, batch], exporters: [otlp]}
```
Grant `otel-collector` SA the `tempostack-traces-write` ClusterRole for tenant `prod`.
Production notes: install Tempo/OTel only if applications emit traces; COO is needed regardless for the logging console view.

