## 5. GitOps & CI/CD

### 5.1 OpenShift GitOps (Argo CD)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Declarative, Git-driven management of cluster configuration and applications. The default `openshift-gitops` Argo CD instance is intended for **cluster config** (operators, RBAC, quotas, policies); teams get their own Argo CD instances for apps. Provides drift detection, sync waves, and audit history for every change. |
| **Package** | `openshift-gitops-operator` |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-gitops-operator` / all namespaces |
| **Channel** | `latest` or `gitops-1.18` (pin to a specific channel in prod) |
| **Primary CRs** | `ArgoCD`, `Application`, `ApplicationSet`, `AppProject` |

```yaml
# Harden the default cluster-config instance
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1beta1
kind: ArgoCD
metadata: {name: openshift-gitops, namespace: openshift-gitops}
spec:
  server:
    route: {enabled: true, tls: {termination: reencrypt}}
    autoscale: {enabled: true}
  sso:
    provider: dex
    dex: {openShiftOAuth: true}
  rbac:
    defaultPolicy: role:readonly
    policy: |
      g, ocp-cluster-admins, role:admin
      g, ocp-platform-team, role:admin
    scopes: "[groups]"
  controller:
    resources: {requests: {cpu: 500m, memory: 1Gi}, limits: {cpu: "2", memory: 4Gi}}
  repo:
    resources: {requests: {cpu: 250m, memory: 512Mi}, limits: {cpu: "1", memory: 1Gi}}
  resourceHealthChecks: []
  nodePlacement:
    nodeSelector: {node-role.kubernetes.io/infra: ""}
    tolerations:
      - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoSchedule}
      - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoExecute}
---
# Cluster-config app-of-apps
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata: {name: cluster-config, namespace: openshift-gitops}
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: https://git.example.com/platform/ocp-prod-config.git
    targetRevision: main
    path: clusters/ocp-prod
  destination: {server: https://kubernetes.default.svc}
  syncPolicy:
    automated: {prune: false, selfHeal: true}
    syncOptions: [CreateNamespace=true, ServerSideApply=true]
```
```bash
oc adm policy add-cluster-role-to-user cluster-admin -z openshift-gitops-argocd-application-controller -n openshift-gitops
oc create secret generic git-creds -n openshift-gitops --from-literal=url=https://git.example.com --from-literal=username=svc-argocd --from-literal=password=<token>
oc label secret git-creds -n openshift-gitops argocd.argoproj.io/secret-type=repo-creds
```
Production notes: disable the default `openshift-gitops` instance (`DISABLE_DEFAULT_ARGOCD_INSTANCE=true` env on the Subscription) if you manage Argo CD yourself; store the Git CA in `argocd-tls-certs-cm`; never use `prune: true` on cluster-config until well tested.

### 5.2 OpenShift Pipelines (Tekton)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Kubernetes-native CI: `Task`/`Pipeline`/`PipelineRun` CRs executed as pods, with Tekton Triggers for Git webhooks, Tekton Chains for supply-chain signing/attestation (SLSA), Tekton Results for history, and a console UI. Install only if you don't use external CI (Jenkins/GitLab CI/GitHub Actions). |
| **Package** | `openshift-pipelines-operator-rh` |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-operators` / all namespaces |
| **Channel** | `latest` or `pipelines-1.20` (pin in prod) |
| **Primary CRs** | `TektonConfig`, `TektonChain`, `TektonResult` |

```yaml
apiVersion: operator.tekton.dev/v1alpha1
kind: TektonConfig
metadata: {name: config}
spec:
  profile: all
  targetNamespace: openshift-pipelines
  pruner:
    resources: [pipelinerun, taskrun]
    keep: 50
    schedule: "0 3 * * *"
  pipeline:
    default-service-account: pipeline
    enable-api-fields: stable
    disable-affinity-assistant: false
    default-timeout-minutes: 60
    performance: {buckets: 3, replicas: 2}
  chain:
    disabled: false
    artifacts.oci.storage: oci
    artifacts.pipelinerun.format: in-toto
    transparency.enabled: "false"        # disconnected: no public Rekor
  trigger:
    default-service-account: pipeline
  hub:
    params: [{name: enable-devconsole-integration, value: "false"}]   # disconnected
  platforms:
    openshift: {pipelinesAsCode: {enable: true, settings: {}}}
```
```bash
# Point ClusterTasks / resolvers at the mirror registry images
oc patch tektonconfig config --type merge -p '{"spec":{"pipeline":{"default-resolver-type":"bundles"}}}'
```
Production notes: set a `ResourceQuota` in `openshift-pipelines`; use `pipelinesAsCode` with your Git server; mirror the Tekton Hub task bundle images (`registry.redhat.io/openshift-pipelines/*`) in the ImageSetConfiguration `additionalImages`.

